{"id": "wwdc2019-808", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/808", "wordCount": 3887, "segments": [{"start": 10.0, "text": "With iOS 13, the way that we"}, {"start": 12.0, "text": "design and build apps is going"}, {"start": 14.0, "text": "to change in some subtle but"}, {"start": 16.0, "text": "significant ways."}, {"start": 18.0, "text": "Dark Mode brings a new approach"}, {"start": 21.0, "text": "to how we work with colors,"}, {"start": 22.0, "text": "images, and text."}, {"start": 25.0, "text": "The new card-style sheets not"}, {"start": 27.0, "text": "only present modal presentations"}, {"start": 29.0, "text": "in a different way, but they"}, {"start": 31.0, "text": "change how we interact with them"}, {"start": 32.0, "text": "as well."}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "And the new contextual menu"}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "control makes it easy to quickly"}, {"start": 39.0, "text": "access contextually relevant"}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "functionality with ease."}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "Now, between these three topics,"}, {"start": 45.0, "text": "we've got a lot of ground to"}, {"start": 46.0, "text": "cover, so let's dive in with"}, {"start": 48.0, "text": "Dark Mode."}, {"start": 50.0, "text": "Now, last year we introduced"}, {"start": 52.0, "text": "Dark Mode on macOS, and it was"}, {"start": 55.0, "text": "pretty popular."}, {"start": 57.0, "text": "For many years, photo and video"}, {"start": 58.0, "text": "apps have used dark interfaces"}, {"start": 61.0, "text": "because they allow people to see"}, {"start": 62.0, "text": "photos and videos with clarity."}, {"start": 66.0, "text": "Dark UIs are great for dark"}, {"start": 68.0, "text": "lighting conditions; it's much"}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "easier for our eyes to adjust"}, {"start": 72.0, "text": "between a dark screen and the"}, {"start": 73.0, "text": "world around us."}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "And, functional reasons aside,"}, {"start": 78.0, "text": "some people just prefer dark"}, {"start": 79.0, "text": "interfaces as a matter of"}, {"start": 81.0, "text": "personal preference."}, {"start": 84.0, "text": "Dark Mode on iOS uses a fully"}, {"start": 86.0, "text": "black background to provide"}, {"start": 88.0, "text": "maximal contrast with text and"}, {"start": 90.0, "text": "other foreground elements."}, {"start": 93.0, "text": "Black backgrounds blend in"}, {"start": 95.0, "text": "seamlessly with the hardware"}, {"start": 96.0, "text": "bezel to make your UI feel more"}, {"start": 98.0, "text": "expansive and integrated with"}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "the hardware itself."}, {"start": 102.0, "text": "In general, all of your apps"}, {"start": 105.0, "text": "should support Dark Mode."}, {"start": 107.0, "text": "When the people using your app"}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "have set their device to be in"}, {"start": 110.0, "text": "Dark Mode, they'll expect your"}, {"start": 111.0, "text": "app to change as well."}, {"start": 114.0, "text": "Now, supporting Dark Mode"}, {"start": 115.0, "text": "involves moving towards the"}, {"start": 117.0, "text": "updated iOS design system which"}, {"start": 120.0, "text": "has been fully overhauled for"}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "iOS 13."}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "Now, just so we're all on the"}, {"start": 125.0, "text": "same page, \"design system\""}, {"start": 127.0, "text": "basically just means a set of"}, {"start": 128.0, "text": "parts like colors, fonts, and"}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "glyphs that work together in a"}, {"start": 133.0, "text": "logical and consistent manor."}, {"start": 136.0, "text": "A rational -- excuse me -- and"}, {"start": 139.0, "text": "consistent design system helps"}, {"start": 140.0, "text": "people to learn and use apps"}, {"start": 143.0, "text": "with ease."}, {"start": 144.0, "text": "By integrating with the iOS"}, {"start": 146.0, "text": "design system, your app will"}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "feel more familiar to people and"}, {"start": 151.0, "text": "be more understandable."}, {"start": 153.0, "text": "Now, before we get into all of"}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "the details, I'd like to share"}, {"start": 156.0, "text": "some of the key design goals"}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "that guided the design team's"}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "efforts."}, {"start": 162.0, "text": "First and foremost, they wanted"}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "iOS to remain familiar and"}, {"start": 166.0, "text": "intuitive."}, {"start": 167.0, "text": "The iOS design system has"}, {"start": 169.0, "text": "received a complete makeover but"}, {"start": 171.0, "text": "the end result is still"}, {"start": 173.0, "text": "recognizably iOS."}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "They sought to provide more"}, {"start": 178.0, "text": "internal consistency."}, {"start": 180.0, "text": "All of the built-in apps were"}, {"start": 182.0, "text": "redesigned to bring them into"}, {"start": 184.0, "text": "alignment with each other, using"}, {"start": 186.0, "text": "all of the components that we'll"}, {"start": 187.0, "text": "be talking about with you today."}, {"start": 190.0, "text": "They also wanted the new design"}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "system to include a range of"}, {"start": 193.0, "text": "color options to help"}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "successfully articulate"}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "information hierarchy, to allow"}, {"start": 199.0, "text": "the most important elements to"}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "be the strongest and the less"}, {"start": 203.0, "text": "important elements to recede."}, {"start": 205.0, "text": "They also put accessibility on"}, {"start": 207.0, "text": "equal footing with these other"}, {"start": 209.0, "text": "goals."}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "The new system fully supports"}, {"start": 212.0, "text": "bold text and increased contrast"}, {"start": 215.0, "text": "accessibility modes."}, {"start": 218.0, "text": "And, lastly, they wanted the new"}, {"start": 220.0, "text": "design system to be simple,"}, {"start": 222.0, "text": "straightforward, and easy to"}, {"start": 224.0, "text": "implement."}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "All right, now let's get into"}, {"start": 227.0, "text": "the specifics."}, {"start": 229.0, "text": "Color seems like the right place"}, {"start": 231.0, "text": "to start."}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "Every app has a background, and"}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "most apps have text and glyphs."}, {"start": 239.0, "text": "And some apps have separator"}, {"start": 240.0, "text": "lines and grouping boxes to help"}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "organize all of that content."}, {"start": 247.0, "text": "Now, when describing these"}, {"start": 248.0, "text": "colors, we can naturally talk"}, {"start": 250.0, "text": "about them by their values."}, {"start": 252.0, "text": "The text is black, the"}, {"start": 254.0, "text": "background is white, etc., etc."}, {"start": 257.0, "text": "Now, as your interface gets a"}, {"start": 259.0, "text": "little bit more complicated, the"}, {"start": 260.0, "text": "length of that color palette"}, {"start": 262.0, "text": "extends."}, {"start": 263.0, "text": "But that's not really an issue."}, {"start": 266.0, "text": "However, when you add support"}, {"start": 268.0, "text": "for separate appearance, you now"}, {"start": 271.0, "text": "have two parallel sets of colors"}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "to keep in sync with each other"}, {"start": 275.0, "text": "and manage."}, {"start": 277.0, "text": "At this point, it becomes"}, {"start": 278.0, "text": "helpful to think about color in"}, {"start": 280.0, "text": "a more abstract way."}, {"start": 282.0, "text": "This is where semantic colors"}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "comes in."}, {"start": 286.0, "text": "A semantic color describes the"}, {"start": 288.0, "text": "purpose of a color rather than"}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "what its value is."}, {"start": 293.0, "text": "Because semantic colors are"}, {"start": 294.0, "text": "extracted away from their exact"}, {"start": 296.0, "text": "appearance, they can work both"}, {"start": 299.0, "text": "-- they're dynamic."}, {"start": 301.0, "text": "So, a background color can be"}, {"start": 303.0, "text": "black in Dark Mode and white in"}, {"start": 305.0, "text": "Light Mode."}, {"start": 307.0, "text": "So instead of maintaining two"}, {"start": 309.0, "text": "separate lists of colors for"}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "Light and Dark Modes, you can"}, {"start": 312.0, "text": "apply semantic colors from the"}, {"start": 314.0, "text": "system palette to UI elements"}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "and their appearance will automatically adapt between"}, {"start": 319.0, "text": "Light and Dark Modes, which is"}, {"start": 321.0, "text": "pretty convenient."}, {"start": 323.0, "text": "iOS 13 includes a palette of"}, {"start": 326.0, "text": "semantic colors for you to use."}, {"start": 328.0, "text": "Many of these colors have"}, {"start": 330.0, "text": "primary, secondary, tertiary,"}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "and quaternary values."}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "These variants are used to"}, {"start": 336.0, "text": "express information hierarchy."}, {"start": 339.0, "text": "Label color has the most"}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "contrast with the background, so"}, {"start": 342.0, "text": "it's going to advance into the"}, {"start": 343.0, "text": "foreground and grab your"}, {"start": 344.0, "text": "attention and should be used for"}, {"start": 346.0, "text": "primary elements like titles,"}, {"start": 348.0, "text": "secondary for subtitles,"}, {"start": 351.0, "text": "tertiary for placeholder text,"}, {"start": 352.0, "text": "quaternary for disabled text."}, {"start": 356.0, "text": "The same basic principle applies"}, {"start": 357.0, "text": "to background colors."}, {"start": 359.0, "text": "System background is a primary"}, {"start": 361.0, "text": "background color, and it's pure"}, {"start": 362.0, "text": "white in Light Mode and Pure"}, {"start": 364.0, "text": "Black in Dark Mode."}, {"start": 365.0, "text": "Secondary and tertiary system"}, {"start": 368.0, "text": "background colors allow you to"}, {"start": 370.0, "text": "structure information"}, {"start": 371.0, "text": "hierarchically."}, {"start": 373.0, "text": "There's also a parallel set of"}, {"start": 375.0, "text": "background colors for grouped"}, {"start": 377.0, "text": "table views."}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "Now, if you observe closely,"}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "you'll note that the colors"}, {"start": 382.0, "text": "aren't simply inverted between"}, {"start": 384.0, "text": "Light and Dark Modes."}, {"start": 385.0, "text": "The table row backgrounds are"}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "lighter in both."}, {"start": 389.0, "text": "There was a concerted effort to"}, {"start": 390.0, "text": "select a palette of colors that"}, {"start": 392.0, "text": "assured contrast while at the"}, {"start": 394.0, "text": "same time keeping apps looking"}, {"start": 397.0, "text": "similar between Light and Dark"}, {"start": 398.0, "text": "Modes."}, {"start": 400.0, "text": "When you're designing for Dark"}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "Mode, it's often helpful to"}, {"start": 403.0, "text": "think about the lights as having"}, {"start": 405.0, "text": "been dimmed rather than"}, {"start": 406.0, "text": "everything being flipped inside"}, {"start": 409.0, "text": "out."}, {"start": 410.0, "text": "The new system palette includes"}, {"start": 412.0, "text": "fill colors and separator"}, {"start": 413.0, "text": "colors."}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "All of the fill colors and one"}, {"start": 416.0, "text": "of the separator colors are"}, {"start": 417.0, "text": "semi-transparent, which helps"}, {"start": 420.0, "text": "them to contrast well against"}, {"start": 422.0, "text": "variable background colors."}, {"start": 425.0, "text": "The new palette includes six,"}, {"start": 427.0, "text": "fully opaque gray values."}, {"start": 429.0, "text": "These colors are best used when"}, {"start": 431.0, "text": "transparency would lead to"}, {"start": 432.0, "text": "undesirable results."}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "So, for example, when drawing"}, {"start": 436.0, "text": "intersecting grid lines,"}, {"start": 438.0, "text": "overlapping semi-transparent"}, {"start": 440.0, "text": "colors can create distracting"}, {"start": 442.0, "text": "optical illusions."}, {"start": 444.0, "text": "And, if elements overlap, solid"}, {"start": 446.0, "text": "colors are really helpful and"}, {"start": 448.0, "text": "prevent things from looking"}, {"start": 450.0, "text": "disabled or broken."}, {"start": 452.0, "text": "These colors are used throughout"}, {"start": 454.0, "text": "the system for basically"}, {"start": 456.0, "text": "everything, and we encourage you"}, {"start": 458.0, "text": "to use them in your apps."}, {"start": 460.0, "text": "To get you started, you can"}, {"start": 462.0, "text": "check out the full color palette"}, {"start": 464.0, "text": "in the Apple Design Resources"}, {"start": 465.0, "text": "and the Human Interface"}, {"start": 466.0, "text": "Guidelines."}, {"start": 468.0, "text": "I'll have more information about"}, {"start": 469.0, "text": "those at the end of the"}, {"start": 470.0, "text": "presentation."}, {"start": 472.0, "text": "As before, we will continue to"}, {"start": 473.0, "text": "provide tint colors for you to"}, {"start": 475.0, "text": "use as your app's tint color."}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "These tint colors are dynamic,"}, {"start": 480.0, "text": "meaning that they have variants"}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "for Light and Dark Modes."}, {"start": 484.0, "text": "Each tint color has"}, {"start": 485.0, "text": "high-contrast variants."}, {"start": 487.0, "text": "When they increase contrast,"}, {"start": 489.0, "text": "accessibility setting is"}, {"start": 490.0, "text": "enabled."}, {"start": 492.0, "text": "Tint colors get lighter in Dark"}, {"start": 494.0, "text": "Mode and darker in Light Mode."}, {"start": 498.0, "text": "Now, if you opt to pick your own"}, {"start": 500.0, "text": "tint color, try to select colors"}, {"start": 502.0, "text": "that work well in both modes."}, {"start": 505.0, "text": "A color that works well in Light"}, {"start": 507.0, "text": "Mode, though, might have"}, {"start": 508.0, "text": "insufficient contrast in Dark"}, {"start": 510.0, "text": "Mode, and vice versa."}, {"start": 513.0, "text": "Even when colors seem to you"}, {"start": 515.0, "text": "like they're going to work well"}, {"start": 516.0, "text": "in both modes, it's always best"}, {"start": 518.0, "text": "to check your colors with an"}, {"start": 520.0, "text": "online color contrast"}, {"start": 521.0, "text": "calculator."}, {"start": 523.0, "text": "Now, because tint colors can be"}, {"start": 524.0, "text": "dynamic, you can have two"}, {"start": 527.0, "text": "slightly different colors for"}, {"start": 528.0, "text": "Light and Dark Modes, and when"}, {"start": 531.0, "text": "you're picking those colors, aim"}, {"start": 532.0, "text": "for a contrast ratio of 4.5 to 1"}, {"start": 536.0, "text": "or higher."}, {"start": 537.0, "text": "Strong color contrast improves"}, {"start": 540.0, "text": "the accessibility and usability"}, {"start": 542.0, "text": "of your apps."}, {"start": 544.0, "text": "The system palette should"}, {"start": 546.0, "text": "basically have you covered for"}, {"start": 548.0, "text": "most of your needs."}, {"start": 549.0, "text": "But, of course, you're going to"}, {"start": 551.0, "text": "have to define your own colors"}, {"start": 552.0, "text": "as well."}, {"start": 554.0, "text": "Perhaps you have user-selectable"}, {"start": 556.0, "text": "label colors or status"}, {"start": 557.0, "text": "indicators."}, {"start": 559.0, "text": "As with tint colors, any color"}, {"start": 560.0, "text": "can be dynamic."}, {"start": 562.0, "text": "Given that the perception of"}, {"start": 564.0, "text": "color is influenced by the"}, {"start": 565.0, "text": "background that it's shown"}, {"start": 566.0, "text": "against, you'll want to make"}, {"start": 568.0, "text": "some adjustments to help keep"}, {"start": 570.0, "text": "those color values looking"}, {"start": 572.0, "text": "similar between modes or to make"}, {"start": 575.0, "text": "sure that there's enough"}, {"start": 576.0, "text": "contrast in both modes."}, {"start": 579.0, "text": "Now, all this time I've been"}, {"start": 580.0, "text": "talking about Light and Dark"}, {"start": 582.0, "text": "Modes, and as you may know,"}, {"start": 584.0, "text": "that's a little bit of an"}, {"start": 585.0, "text": "oversimplification."}, {"start": 586.0, "text": "There's actually two sets of"}, {"start": 588.0, "text": "background colors that are"}, {"start": 589.0, "text": "called \"base\" and \"elevated.\""}, {"start": 593.0, "text": "As the names imply, these"}, {"start": 595.0, "text": "background colors are about"}, {"start": 596.0, "text": "layering interfaces."}, {"start": 599.0, "text": "When two light interfaces are"}, {"start": 601.0, "text": "layered, a simple, diffuse drop"}, {"start": 604.0, "text": "shadow is all you need to create"}, {"start": 606.0, "text": "visual separation between the"}, {"start": 607.0, "text": "two."}, {"start": 608.0, "text": "With dark interfaces, drop"}, {"start": 610.0, "text": "shadows are slightly less"}, {"start": 612.0, "text": "effective."}, {"start": 615.0, "text": "System background colors will"}, {"start": 617.0, "text": "use the darker or base values"}, {"start": 619.0, "text": "for background apps or"}, {"start": 620.0, "text": "interfaces and the lighter,"}, {"start": 622.0, "text": "elevated values for apps or"}, {"start": 624.0, "text": "interfaces that are in the"}, {"start": 626.0, "text": "foreground."}, {"start": 627.0, "text": "So take, for example, the"}, {"start": 629.0, "text": "Contacts app."}, {"start": 630.0, "text": "It's using the base set of color"}, {"start": 631.0, "text": "values when drawn on its own,"}, {"start": 633.0, "text": "but when the same interface is"}, {"start": 635.0, "text": "brought up in a modal"}, {"start": 636.0, "text": "presentation in the phone app,"}, {"start": 638.0, "text": "it uses the elevated background"}, {"start": 640.0, "text": "colors."}, {"start": 641.0, "text": "Okay, let's look at a slightly"}, {"start": 643.0, "text": "more complicated example."}, {"start": 645.0, "text": "Here's Mail running on an iPad."}, {"start": 647.0, "text": "On its own, Mail is drawn using"}, {"start": 650.0, "text": "the base set of background"}, {"start": 651.0, "text": "colors."}, {"start": 652.0, "text": "When we bring in Contacts in a"}, {"start": 654.0, "text": "slide-over, we see that it's"}, {"start": 656.0, "text": "being drawn with the elevated"}, {"start": 657.0, "text": "set of background colors."}, {"start": 659.0, "text": "Now, the lighter appearance of"}, {"start": 662.0, "text": "contacts helps it stand out from"}, {"start": 664.0, "text": "Mail and advances it into the"}, {"start": 666.0, "text": "foreground."}, {"start": 667.0, "text": "When Contacts is displayed side"}, {"start": 671.0, "text": "by side in multitasking with"}, {"start": 672.0, "text": "Mail, they are both drawn with"}, {"start": 675.0, "text": "the elevated set of background"}, {"start": 676.0, "text": "colors."}, {"start": 677.0, "text": "This helps provide contrast with"}, {"start": 679.0, "text": "that splitter down the middle"}, {"start": 681.0, "text": "and keeps the two apps from"}, {"start": 682.0, "text": "blending together."}, {"start": 684.0, "text": "When we compose an email in"}, {"start": 687.0, "text": "Mail, it comes up in a sheet."}, {"start": 689.0, "text": "This too is drawn with the"}, {"start": 691.0, "text": "elevated background colors, but"}, {"start": 693.0, "text": "the main app UI Mail looks a"}, {"start": 695.0, "text": "little bit darker because modal"}, {"start": 697.0, "text": "presentations draw an overlay"}, {"start": 699.0, "text": "layer to dim their background"}, {"start": 701.0, "text": "content and they cast a little"}, {"start": 703.0, "text": "bit of a drop shadow."}, {"start": 705.0, "text": "Now, because background colors"}, {"start": 707.0, "text": "change when your app is"}, {"start": 708.0, "text": "elevated, you have to be mindful"}, {"start": 710.0, "text": "that some of the darker colors"}, {"start": 712.0, "text": "that you might use, even from"}, {"start": 713.0, "text": "the system palette, may not"}, {"start": 715.0, "text": "contrast well."}, {"start": 716.0, "text": "You always have to check your"}, {"start": 718.0, "text": "designs when they're in elevated"}, {"start": 720.0, "text": "state."}, {"start": 722.0, "text": "Again, semi-opaque fill and"}, {"start": 724.0, "text": "separator colors are going to be"}, {"start": 726.0, "text": "your best friends here."}, {"start": 727.0, "text": "They adapt gracefully between"}, {"start": 729.0, "text": "base and elevated backgrounds."}, {"start": 732.0, "text": "Okay, moving on to materials."}, {"start": 736.0, "text": "Materials have been overhauled"}, {"start": 738.0, "text": "and refined with iOS 13."}, {"start": 740.0, "text": "There are now four materials for"}, {"start": 742.0, "text": "you to choose from with a range"}, {"start": 744.0, "text": "of translucency levels: thick,"}, {"start": 747.0, "text": "regular, thin, and ultra-thin."}, {"start": 750.0, "text": "These materials have been"}, {"start": 753.0, "text": "designed to work well against a"}, {"start": 754.0, "text": "variety of background contexts."}, {"start": 757.0, "text": "Their appearance will change"}, {"start": 759.0, "text": "dynamically based on whether"}, {"start": 761.0, "text": "someone is using your app in"}, {"start": 762.0, "text": "Light or Dark Mode."}, {"start": 764.0, "text": "You can select which material"}, {"start": 765.0, "text": "you want based on how much"}, {"start": 767.0, "text": "separation you want from the"}, {"start": 768.0, "text": "background, how much is most"}, {"start": 770.0, "text": "appropriate."}, {"start": 772.0, "text": "The default material is regular,"}, {"start": 774.0, "text": "and it's going to work well in"}, {"start": 775.0, "text": "most circumstances."}, {"start": 777.0, "text": "But if you're presenting content"}, {"start": 779.0, "text": "against this material that needs"}, {"start": 781.0, "text": "a little bit more contrast, you"}, {"start": 783.0, "text": "can use the thicker material."}, {"start": 785.0, "text": "For lighter-weight interactions,"}, {"start": 787.0, "text": "maybe with simpler content, thin"}, {"start": 790.0, "text": "and ultra-thin might be the"}, {"start": 791.0, "text": "right way to go."}, {"start": 792.0, "text": "Which material is right for your"}, {"start": 794.0, "text": "app just really depends on the"}, {"start": 795.0, "text": "content that's being displayed"}, {"start": 797.0, "text": "inside of it."}, {"start": 799.0, "text": "Speaking of which, light and"}, {"start": 801.0, "text": "dark materials have an"}, {"start": 802.0, "text": "accompanying set of vibrancy"}, {"start": 804.0, "text": "values for labels, fills, and"}, {"start": 806.0, "text": "separator colors."}, {"start": 808.0, "text": "Vibrancy is a visual affect"}, {"start": 809.0, "text": "that's used throughout iOS and"}, {"start": 811.0, "text": "other Apple platforms."}, {"start": 813.0, "text": "With system materials, it's"}, {"start": 815.0, "text": "typically best to use vibrancy"}, {"start": 818.0, "text": "rather than solid colors."}, {"start": 820.0, "text": "Because depending on the"}, {"start": 821.0, "text": "background context, solid colors"}, {"start": 823.0, "text": "can get really muddy and can"}, {"start": 825.0, "text": "lead to some serious legibility"}, {"start": 827.0, "text": "issues."}, {"start": 829.0, "text": "Vibrancy helps to maintain that"}, {"start": 831.0, "text": "contrast regardless of what's in"}, {"start": 833.0, "text": "the background."}, {"start": 834.0, "text": "The updated visual design system"}, {"start": 836.0, "text": "for iOS also includes changes to"}, {"start": 839.0, "text": "controls and bars."}, {"start": 842.0, "text": "Visual attributes like shape and"}, {"start": 845.0, "text": "color have been brought into"}, {"start": 847.0, "text": "greater alignment for more"}, {"start": 848.0, "text": "internal consistency."}, {"start": 851.0, "text": "Controls are now drawn with"}, {"start": 853.0, "text": "semantic colors so that they"}, {"start": 855.0, "text": "gracefully adapt between Light"}, {"start": 857.0, "text": "and Dark Modes."}, {"start": 859.0, "text": "If you use UIKit controls, you"}, {"start": 862.0, "text": "get the benefits of all of this"}, {"start": 863.0, "text": "for free."}, {"start": 865.0, "text": "If you spent time recreating"}, {"start": 867.0, "text": "what UIKit gives you for free,"}, {"start": 869.0, "text": "with custom controls, you may"}, {"start": 871.0, "text": "want to, I don't know how to say"}, {"start": 873.0, "text": "this, but stop doing that."}, {"start": 882.0, "text": "Recreating what UIKit gives you"}, {"start": 885.0, "text": "for free takes a lot of effort"}, {"start": 887.0, "text": "and time, it's hard to do right,"}, {"start": 889.0, "text": "and there's very little upside"}, {"start": 890.0, "text": "for you."}, {"start": 892.0, "text": "But of course, custom controls"}, {"start": 894.0, "text": "are often necessary."}, {"start": 896.0, "text": "UIKit does not provide"}, {"start": 897.0, "text": "everything that you need."}, {"start": 899.0, "text": "For example, UIKit doesn't"}, {"start": 900.0, "text": "provide a rating indicator."}, {"start": 902.0, "text": "So, when you're making custom"}, {"start": 903.0, "text": "controls, you should use the"}, {"start": 905.0, "text": "system palette so that you don't"}, {"start": 908.0, "text": "have to do two different color"}, {"start": 909.0, "text": "treatments for Light and Dark"}, {"start": 910.0, "text": "Mode."}, {"start": 912.0, "text": "Navigation bars have also been"}, {"start": 914.0, "text": "updated."}, {"start": 916.0, "text": "By default, they're now drawn"}, {"start": 917.0, "text": "for large titles without the"}, {"start": 919.0, "text": "background and shadow."}, {"start": 922.0, "text": "This allows the title to connect"}, {"start": 924.0, "text": "seamlessly with the content that"}, {"start": 926.0, "text": "it's labeling."}, {"start": 927.0, "text": "When content scrolls underneath"}, {"start": 930.0, "text": "the navigation bar, the"}, {"start": 932.0, "text": "background and shadow will fade"}, {"start": 933.0, "text": "back in."}, {"start": 935.0, "text": "Now, large title bars,"}, {"start": 937.0, "text": "navigation bars work especially"}, {"start": 938.0, "text": "well with this visual treatment,"}, {"start": 940.0, "text": "but it can be used for default"}, {"start": 942.0, "text": "navigation bars as well."}, {"start": 944.0, "text": "So, in the Settings app, for"}, {"start": 945.0, "text": "example, the master view's"}, {"start": 947.0, "text": "navigation bar uses a large"}, {"start": 949.0, "text": "title and it has no background"}, {"start": 951.0, "text": "or shadow."}, {"start": 952.0, "text": "The standard navigation bar is"}, {"start": 954.0, "text": "stylized to match."}, {"start": 957.0, "text": "Now, while a seamless navigation"}, {"start": 959.0, "text": "bar looks great, it's not always"}, {"start": 961.0, "text": "going to be appropriate."}, {"start": 963.0, "text": "That background is completely"}, {"start": 964.0, "text": "transparent, so if you've tucked"}, {"start": 966.0, "text": "anything underneath the"}, {"start": 967.0, "text": "navigation bar, it's going to"}, {"start": 968.0, "text": "show right through, and it's"}, {"start": 970.0, "text": "probably not going to look very"}, {"start": 971.0, "text": "good so don't use a treatment"}, {"start": 973.0, "text": "then."}, {"start": 974.0, "text": "And if you have a really dense"}, {"start": 976.0, "text": "interface with a lot of controls"}, {"start": 977.0, "text": "and navigation bar next to the"}, {"start": 979.0, "text": "content area, the clear visual"}, {"start": 981.0, "text": "delineation that's provided by"}, {"start": 983.0, "text": "that shadow can be really"}, {"start": 984.0, "text": "helpful."}, {"start": 986.0, "text": "Okay. So, before we move on,"}, {"start": 988.0, "text": "there's one more big feature"}, {"start": 990.0, "text": "that I'd like to discuss with"}, {"start": 991.0, "text": "you related to Dark Mode."}, {"start": 994.0, "text": "iOS has always provided a"}, {"start": 996.0, "text": "handful of symbols for things"}, {"start": 997.0, "text": "like table rows and toolbars."}, {"start": 1000.0, "text": "When shown against a dark"}, {"start": 1001.0, "text": "background, the previous set of"}, {"start": 1003.0, "text": "symbols did not hold up very"}, {"start": 1005.0, "text": "well; they often looked a little"}, {"start": 1007.0, "text": "too thin."}, {"start": 1009.0, "text": "So, the design team redesigned"}, {"start": 1012.0, "text": "all of the symbols in this"}, {"start": 1014.0, "text": "design system."}, {"start": 1015.0, "text": "And what's really cool, as many"}, {"start": 1017.0, "text": "of you may know already, we're"}, {"start": 1019.0, "text": "making all of those glyphs"}, {"start": 1020.0, "text": "available for you to use with SF"}, {"start": 1022.0, "text": "Symbols."}, {"start": 1024.0, "text": "SF Symbols includes over 1500"}, {"start": 1027.0, "text": "symbols."}, {"start": 1028.0, "text": "And this isn't just a new set of"}, {"start": 1030.0, "text": "glyphs; this represents a"}, {"start": 1032.0, "text": "completely new way to think"}, {"start": 1034.0, "text": "about and design glyphs."}, {"start": 1037.0, "text": "As the name suggests, SF Symbols"}, {"start": 1039.0, "text": "are designed to match the visual"}, {"start": 1041.0, "text": "design characteristics of San"}, {"start": 1044.0, "text": "Francisco, the system font for"}, {"start": 1046.0, "text": "iOS and other Apple platforms."}, {"start": 1049.0, "text": "They can literally be typed out"}, {"start": 1052.0, "text": "so that they can be displayed"}, {"start": 1053.0, "text": "inline with text."}, {"start": 1055.0, "text": "They have imbedded baseline"}, {"start": 1057.0, "text": "values to assure proper vertical"}, {"start": 1059.0, "text": "alignment relative to text."}, {"start": 1061.0, "text": "And every SF symbol offers"}, {"start": 1063.0, "text": "small, medium and large-scale"}, {"start": 1066.0, "text": "variants relative to the current"}, {"start": 1068.0, "text": "size for different contexts."}, {"start": 1071.0, "text": "And every symbol comes in nine"}, {"start": 1072.0, "text": "weights just like the SF font."}, {"start": 1075.0, "text": "Because they're vector based, SF"}, {"start": 1077.0, "text": "Symbols can scale with text when"}, {"start": 1080.0, "text": "used with dynamic type."}, {"start": 1083.0, "text": "And by offering multiple"}, {"start": 1085.0, "text": "weights, SF Symbols will become"}, {"start": 1087.0, "text": "bolder when the bold text"}, {"start": 1089.0, "text": "accessibility setting is"}, {"start": 1091.0, "text": "enabled."}, {"start": 1093.0, "text": "Now, when designing comps of"}, {"start": 1094.0, "text": "your app, you can use the new SF"}, {"start": 1097.0, "text": "Symbols app to browse or search"}, {"start": 1099.0, "text": "for symbols, copy the ones that"}, {"start": 1101.0, "text": "you want to use, go over to your"}, {"start": 1103.0, "text": "design comp, and just paste them"}, {"start": 1105.0, "text": "in to a text layer."}, {"start": 1106.0, "text": "The updated iOS Apple Design"}, {"start": 1109.0, "text": "Resources for Sketch is already"}, {"start": 1112.0, "text": "set up to work with symbols."}, {"start": 1114.0, "text": "To swap out the symbols for this"}, {"start": 1116.0, "text": "tab bar, for example, you just"}, {"start": 1118.0, "text": "select the tab bar, go to the"}, {"start": 1120.0, "text": "inspector, and paste it in to an"}, {"start": 1123.0, "text": "override for the buttons."}, {"start": 1125.0, "text": "I've been playing with this"}, {"start": 1126.0, "text": "feature for a few months now,"}, {"start": 1129.0, "text": "and I have to tell you, it's"}, {"start": 1130.0, "text": "totally game-changing."}, {"start": 1132.0, "text": "Now, if the set of symbols that"}, {"start": 1134.0, "text": "we provide, 1500, isn't enough,"}, {"start": 1136.0, "text": "you can actually generate a"}, {"start": 1137.0, "text": "template in SVG, go into"}, {"start": 1139.0, "text": "Illustrator or Sketch and make"}, {"start": 1141.0, "text": "modifications to design your own"}, {"start": 1143.0, "text": "and get all the same benefits"}, {"start": 1145.0, "text": "that I just described."}, {"start": 1146.0, "text": "It's really cool."}, {"start": 1148.0, "text": "Okay. Now moving on to modal"}, {"start": 1151.0, "text": "presentations."}, {"start": 1153.0, "text": "Modal presentations are often"}, {"start": 1155.0, "text": "called sheets because of the way"}, {"start": 1157.0, "text": "they slide up over the screen."}, {"start": 1159.0, "text": "This animation informs people"}, {"start": 1161.0, "text": "that they've shifted from one"}, {"start": 1163.0, "text": "mode to another or into a new"}, {"start": 1165.0, "text": "modality of your app."}, {"start": 1168.0, "text": "With iOS 13, sheets have a new"}, {"start": 1171.0, "text": "card-like appearance that's used"}, {"start": 1173.0, "text": "throughout the system."}, {"start": 1175.0, "text": "This style is now the default."}, {"start": 1177.0, "text": "And the benefit of this style is"}, {"start": 1179.0, "text": "that it gives this little peek"}, {"start": 1181.0, "text": "of what's in the background,"}, {"start": 1183.0, "text": "which is a helpful reminder that"}, {"start": 1185.0, "text": "there's a different UI that"}, {"start": 1186.0, "text": "accommodates a different task or"}, {"start": 1188.0, "text": "mode of the app that's still in"}, {"start": 1189.0, "text": "the background."}, {"start": 1191.0, "text": "With the full-screen modal"}, {"start": 1192.0, "text": "sheet, you can sometimes forget"}, {"start": 1195.0, "text": "what you were doing before."}, {"start": 1196.0, "text": "Card-style modal sheets can be"}, {"start": 1199.0, "text": "dismissed by swiping down"}, {"start": 1201.0, "text": "anywhere on the screen."}, {"start": 1202.0, "text": "And that dismiss gesture is"}, {"start": 1204.0, "text": "often going to be easier than"}, {"start": 1205.0, "text": "tapping a button in the"}, {"start": 1207.0, "text": "navigation bar."}, {"start": 1209.0, "text": "As with swiping to go back,"}, {"start": 1211.0, "text": "pulling down to dismiss"}, {"start": 1212.0, "text": "facilitates one-handed"}, {"start": 1214.0, "text": "operation, which is particularly"}, {"start": 1216.0, "text": "convenient on devices with"}, {"start": 1217.0, "text": "larger displays."}, {"start": 1219.0, "text": "Now, you may wonder, \"How does"}, {"start": 1221.0, "text": "this work with scrolling?\""}, {"start": 1223.0, "text": "When the content area has been"}, {"start": 1224.0, "text": "scrolled, swiping down will"}, {"start": 1227.0, "text": "scroll it back to the top."}, {"start": 1229.0, "text": "When scrolled all the way back"}, {"start": 1230.0, "text": "to the top, continuing to swipe"}, {"start": 1232.0, "text": "will dismiss the modal"}, {"start": 1233.0, "text": "presentation."}, {"start": 1235.0, "text": "But at any time, you can pull"}, {"start": 1237.0, "text": "down from the top edge of the"}, {"start": 1238.0, "text": "card to dismiss."}, {"start": 1241.0, "text": "Now, if this gesture is"}, {"start": 1243.0, "text": "problematic for any reason, like"}, {"start": 1245.0, "text": "you have a control in the"}, {"start": 1246.0, "text": "content area that works with"}, {"start": 1248.0, "text": "vertical swiping, it can be"}, {"start": 1250.0, "text": "prevented."}, {"start": 1251.0, "text": "It can also be prevented when"}, {"start": 1253.0, "text": "there's a mandatory decision"}, {"start": 1255.0, "text": "that's required in the modal"}, {"start": 1257.0, "text": "presentation itself."}, {"start": 1259.0, "text": "So, for example, here we either"}, {"start": 1260.0, "text": "need to cancel or add."}, {"start": 1263.0, "text": "And if we pull down, it will"}, {"start": 1264.0, "text": "just bounce right back."}, {"start": 1267.0, "text": "In cases where people must make"}, {"start": 1269.0, "text": "a decision before leaving a"}, {"start": 1271.0, "text": "modal context, you can prevent"}, {"start": 1273.0, "text": "that dismiss gesture and display"}, {"start": 1275.0, "text": "an action sheet asking people"}, {"start": 1277.0, "text": "how they wish to proceed, which"}, {"start": 1279.0, "text": "is actually pretty convenient."}, {"start": 1282.0, "text": "Now, in case you're wondering,"}, {"start": 1283.0, "text": "all of what I just described"}, {"start": 1285.0, "text": "here doesn't mean that you don't"}, {"start": 1286.0, "text": "need to have buttons for modal"}, {"start": 1288.0, "text": "cards anymore."}, {"start": 1290.0, "text": "Buttons are critical for letting"}, {"start": 1292.0, "text": "people know that they can close"}, {"start": 1293.0, "text": "the modal."}, {"start": 1295.0, "text": "Buttons are also necessary for"}, {"start": 1296.0, "text": "accessibility reasons."}, {"start": 1298.0, "text": "And people might not be familiar"}, {"start": 1299.0, "text": "with using the gesture yet or"}, {"start": 1301.0, "text": "don't want to."}, {"start": 1302.0, "text": "And when the content area's been"}, {"start": 1303.0, "text": "scrolled down, tapping a button"}, {"start": 1305.0, "text": "might actually be more"}, {"start": 1306.0, "text": "convenient."}, {"start": 1307.0, "text": "Similarly, seeing negative and"}, {"start": 1310.0, "text": "affirmative action pairs at the"}, {"start": 1311.0, "text": "top of the screen lets people"}, {"start": 1313.0, "text": "know what choices they have to"}, {"start": 1315.0, "text": "act within this modal"}, {"start": 1317.0, "text": "presentation, what actions they"}, {"start": 1319.0, "text": "can take."}, {"start": 1320.0, "text": "Now, we think the new card style"}, {"start": 1322.0, "text": "is pretty great, which is why"}, {"start": 1323.0, "text": "it's now the default for iOS."}, {"start": 1326.0, "text": "But they're not always"}, {"start": 1327.0, "text": "appropriate."}, {"start": 1328.0, "text": "For some tasks, like editing a"}, {"start": 1331.0, "text": "picture or marking up a"}, {"start": 1332.0, "text": "screenshot, you really want to"}, {"start": 1334.0, "text": "maximize screen space and"}, {"start": 1336.0, "text": "minimize visual distraction."}, {"start": 1338.0, "text": "For workflows like this, you"}, {"start": 1340.0, "text": "should use the optional"}, {"start": 1341.0, "text": "full-screen presentation."}, {"start": 1343.0, "text": "And one final comment about"}, {"start": 1345.0, "text": "modal presentations: modals are"}, {"start": 1349.0, "text": "for switching modes."}, {"start": 1351.0, "text": "Don't use them just because you"}, {"start": 1352.0, "text": "like the animation or the visual"}, {"start": 1354.0, "text": "style of them."}, {"start": 1356.0, "text": "So, a good example of modal"}, {"start": 1357.0, "text": "sheet use is from Calendar."}, {"start": 1359.0, "text": "Calendar has two primary modes:"}, {"start": 1362.0, "text": "viewing events in a grid or list"}, {"start": 1365.0, "text": "and then creating or editing"}, {"start": 1367.0, "text": "events."}, {"start": 1369.0, "text": "Viewing your calendar involves"}, {"start": 1371.0, "text": "scanning all the events that are"}, {"start": 1373.0, "text": "in your calendar and then"}, {"start": 1374.0, "text": "selecting them to see detail."}, {"start": 1377.0, "text": "Since we're still in the viewing"}, {"start": 1378.0, "text": "mode, a child view is used for"}, {"start": 1380.0, "text": "displaying those details."}, {"start": 1383.0, "text": "As the name suggests, a child is"}, {"start": 1385.0, "text": "an extension of the parent view."}, {"start": 1387.0, "text": "A child view should be a"}, {"start": 1389.0, "text": "continuation of the task or"}, {"start": 1391.0, "text": "workflow that was started in"}, {"start": 1393.0, "text": "that parent view."}, {"start": 1395.0, "text": "When creating or editing an"}, {"start": 1396.0, "text": "event, a modal sheet signals to"}, {"start": 1398.0, "text": "the people who are using"}, {"start": 1399.0, "text": "Calendar that they've switched"}, {"start": 1401.0, "text": "into a distinct and new"}, {"start": 1402.0, "text": "workflow."}, {"start": 1404.0, "text": "Okay. Now for our final iOS"}, {"start": 1406.0, "text": "design topic, and that's"}, {"start": 1408.0, "text": "contextual menus."}, {"start": 1410.0, "text": "With the introduction of 3D"}, {"start": 1413.0, "text": "Touch a few years ago came a new"}, {"start": 1415.0, "text": "interaction called Peek and Pop."}, {"start": 1418.0, "text": "Peek and Pop was primarily about"}, {"start": 1420.0, "text": "getting a larger preview of"}, {"start": 1421.0, "text": "content."}, {"start": 1423.0, "text": "If available, actions could be"}, {"start": 1425.0, "text": "accessed by swiping that preview"}, {"start": 1427.0, "text": "upwards."}, {"start": 1429.0, "text": "Contextual menu shifts things"}, {"start": 1431.0, "text": "around a bit and puts the focus"}, {"start": 1434.0, "text": "on actions."}, {"start": 1436.0, "text": "Actions are presented"}, {"start": 1437.0, "text": "immediately."}, {"start": 1439.0, "text": "Contextual menus also work on"}, {"start": 1441.0, "text": "all devices."}, {"start": 1443.0, "text": "Peek and Pop only worked with 3D"}, {"start": 1445.0, "text": "Touch, so it wasn't available on"}, {"start": 1447.0, "text": "any iPads and some iPhones."}, {"start": 1449.0, "text": "While 3D Touch makes contextual"}, {"start": 1451.0, "text": "menus appear more quickly, the"}, {"start": 1453.0, "text": "gesture to get a contextual menu"}, {"start": 1454.0, "text": "is just tap and hold, and you"}, {"start": 1456.0, "text": "can do that on any touch device."}, {"start": 1458.0, "text": "Contextual menus are comprised"}, {"start": 1460.0, "text": "of two parts: there's a menu of"}, {"start": 1463.0, "text": "commands that can be performed"}, {"start": 1464.0, "text": "on an item or selection, and an"}, {"start": 1467.0, "text": "optional preview of the selected"}, {"start": 1469.0, "text": "item that'll be affected."}, {"start": 1472.0, "text": "That preview can be a helpful"}, {"start": 1473.0, "text": "reminder of what item will be"}, {"start": 1475.0, "text": "affected by those menu of"}, {"start": 1477.0, "text": "commands."}, {"start": 1478.0, "text": "The exact appearance of"}, {"start": 1479.0, "text": "contextual menus will change"}, {"start": 1482.0, "text": "based on device size and"}, {"start": 1483.0, "text": "orientation."}, {"start": 1484.0, "text": "On iPhone, the preview and phone"}, {"start": 1487.0, "text": "are stacked, in portrait, and"}, {"start": 1490.0, "text": "the same thing on iPad when"}, {"start": 1491.0, "text": "there's three commands or fewer."}, {"start": 1493.0, "text": "Otherwise, the menu and preview"}, {"start": 1494.0, "text": "are displayed side by side."}, {"start": 1496.0, "text": "Contextual menus will appear"}, {"start": 1498.0, "text": "directly above the object they"}, {"start": 1499.0, "text": "affect or as close to it as"}, {"start": 1501.0, "text": "possible."}, {"start": 1504.0, "text": "As with macOS contextual menus,"}, {"start": 1506.0, "text": "you can choose the order of menu"}, {"start": 1507.0, "text": "commands."}, {"start": 1509.0, "text": "It's best to put the most"}, {"start": 1510.0, "text": "frequently used or accessed"}, {"start": 1511.0, "text": "commands at the top so that"}, {"start": 1513.0, "text": "they're easier to access."}, {"start": 1515.0, "text": "Otherwise, you should group"}, {"start": 1516.0, "text": "commands because they're heavily"}, {"start": 1518.0, "text": "related with each other."}, {"start": 1520.0, "text": "So, it totally makes sense that"}, {"start": 1521.0, "text": "cut, copy, and paste are near"}, {"start": 1523.0, "text": "each other."}, {"start": 1525.0, "text": "You can also use separators to"}, {"start": 1527.0, "text": "create visually distinct groups."}, {"start": 1530.0, "text": "And iOS contextual menus can be"}, {"start": 1532.0, "text": "hierarchical, meaning that some"}, {"start": 1534.0, "text": "of these options can lead to a"}, {"start": 1536.0, "text": "secondary submenu."}, {"start": 1539.0, "text": "Contextual menus on iOS also"}, {"start": 1541.0, "text": "include glyphs to help people"}, {"start": 1543.0, "text": "find what they're looking for"}, {"start": 1544.0, "text": "more quickly, and they allow you"}, {"start": 1546.0, "text": "to warn people about destructive"}, {"start": 1548.0, "text": "actions by labeling them in red."}, {"start": 1550.0, "text": "You should try to add contextual"}, {"start": 1553.0, "text": "menus to every object in your"}, {"start": 1555.0, "text": "app."}, {"start": 1557.0, "text": "Think about macOS."}, {"start": 1559.0, "text": "You expect every object in every"}, {"start": 1561.0, "text": "app to have a contextual menu."}, {"start": 1564.0, "text": "They're great way to learn what"}, {"start": 1566.0, "text": "actions can be performed on an"}, {"start": 1568.0, "text": "object."}, {"start": 1569.0, "text": "And the more iOS apps add"}, {"start": 1572.0, "text": "contextual menus, the more"}, {"start": 1574.0, "text": "people will expect every app to"}, {"start": 1576.0, "text": "support contextual menus,"}, {"start": 1578.0, "text": "including yours."}, {"start": 1581.0, "text": "Okay, one final comment about"}, {"start": 1583.0, "text": "contextual menus."}, {"start": 1584.0, "text": "The actions they contain should"}, {"start": 1586.0, "text": "still be available somewhere"}, {"start": 1588.0, "text": "else in your main interface."}, {"start": 1590.0, "text": "Contextual menus are powerful"}, {"start": 1592.0, "text": "and convenient, but people might"}, {"start": 1595.0, "text": "not always think to access them."}, {"start": 1598.0, "text": "Now, I can't wait to see what"}, {"start": 1601.0, "text": "you do with Dark Mode, updated"}, {"start": 1603.0, "text": "modal presentations and the new"}, {"start": 1606.0, "text": "contextual menu."}, {"start": 1607.0, "text": "For more information and"}, {"start": 1609.0, "text": "resources, go to"}, {"start": 1610.0, "text": "developer.apple.com/design."}, {"start": 1613.0, "text": "There you can find the updated"}, {"start": 1614.0, "text": "SF font, the SF Symbols app, and"}, {"start": 1617.0, "text": "the updated iOS Design Resources"}, {"start": 1620.0, "text": "for Sketch."}, {"start": 1621.0, "text": "The Adobe Photoshop and Adobe XD"}, {"start": 1623.0, "text": "resources will be coming later"}, {"start": 1625.0, "text": "this summer."}, {"start": 1627.0, "text": "Also, check out the Apple Human"}, {"start": 1630.0, "text": "Interface Guidelines for more"}, {"start": 1631.0, "text": "details about everything that I"}, {"start": 1634.0, "text": "covered today."}]}